  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the project instructions and available tooling, then build the app and verify its API, persistence, browser workflow, and repeatable load exercise within this workspace.",
    "I’m using Python’s standard library with SQLite so the app runs without a separate database service or dependency install. SQLite write transactions will serialize reservation, inventory, audit, and idempotency updates; the UI will be served from the same local process.",
    "The backend and first usable UI are in place. I’m adding route-level tests and a repeatable mixed read/write workload next; those will help catch transaction and retry issues before I exercise the UI in Chromium.",
    "The route suite exposed and helped fix a failure-path transaction cleanup issue. The tests now pass, including reservation contention and a restart check. I’m extending the retry coverage, then I’ll run the benchmark and the browser workflow against the actual server.",
    "The final route suite now covers admin adjustments, draft/reserved cancellation, pagination, repeated-key concurrency, and persisted replay as well as the core fulfillment lifecycle. The browser workflow passed on the live UI. I’m cleaning the temporary verification database and recording the final file/check status now.",
    "Implemented DepotFlow with a persistent SQLite backend, same-origin web UI, route-level tests, and a repeatable load script.\n\n- Start it with `PORT=8000 DATA_DIR=\"$PWD/depot-data\" SEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh`. Demo users and setup details are in [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md).\n- Transaction boundaries, tenant and role checks, retry behavior, and design limits are documented in [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md).\n- Verification passed: Python compilation, all 7 route and persistence tests, and the Chromium operator/viewer workflow.\n- The recorded 500-request benchmark completed with 0 errors: 1,440.6 combined requests/s; read mean latency 2.20 ms and write mean latency 8.31 ms. Methodology and latency percentiles are in the README.\n\nNo known verification failures remain. The documented limits include SQLite’s single-writer behavior and the app’s local-only account and token lifecycle."
  ],
  "final": "Implemented DepotFlow with a persistent SQLite backend, same-origin web UI, route-level tests, and a repeatable load script.\n\n- Start it with `PORT=8000 DATA_DIR=\"$PWD/depot-data\" SEED_DEMO=1 ./run.sh`. Demo users and setup details are in [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md).\n- Transaction boundaries, tenant and role checks, retry behavior, and design limits are documented in [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md).\n- Verification passed: Python compilation, all 7 route and persistence tests, and the Chromium operator/viewer workflow.\n- The recorded 500-request benchmark completed with 0 errors: 1,440.6 combined requests/s; read mean latency 2.20 ms and write mean latency 8.31 ms. Methodology and latency percentiles are in the README.\n\nNo known verification failures remain. The documented limits include SQLite’s single-writer behavior and the app’s local-only account and token lifecycle.",
